{
  "id": "COMPOUND:17155 - PROTEIN:5673",
  "verbalization": "Undecanol is shown to interact with Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, a key enzyme involved in cellular signaling and regulation. This enzyme is targeted by multiple compounds, including [(3S,10S,13R,17R)-17-(5-ethyl-6-methylhept-6-en-2-yl)-4,10,13,14-tetramethyl-1,2,3,4,5,6,9,11,12,15,16,17-dodecahydrocyclopenta[a]phenanthren-3-yl] acetate, methyl 3,4-dihydroxy-5-methoxybenzoate, and sec-butyl acetate, (-). All these compounds have a known target of LS174T, suggesting a common mechanism of action involving the regulation of Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP. The evidence supports a potential role for Undecanol in modulating this pathway, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated. The consistent targeting of Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP by multiple compounds implies that the interaction between Undecanol and LS174T may involve a shared regulatory function, possibly through the inhibition of this enzyme or its downstream signaling.",
